Scan the preset save location for presets

The dialog saves a preset into the generic data location, but it scanned
the generic config location for the preset list. A saved preset therefore
never came back into the list, and the presets that an installation puts
into the data folder stayed hidden.

Scan the data location before the config location. The scan keeps the
first file of each name. A preset in the data location therefore wins,
and a preset in the config folder stays in the list.

The change sits on the branch work/presets of the local tree, as commit 1 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 9abaef8a..bd6344c2 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -1790,9 +1790,12 @@ QtCurveConfig::setupPresets(const Options &currentStyle,
     {
         // Make a unique list of absolute paths
         QHash<QString, QString> files_map;
-        QStringList dirs = QStandardPaths::locateAll(QStandardPaths::GenericConfigLocation,
+        QStringList dirs = QStandardPaths::locateAll(QStandardPaths::GenericDataLocation,
                                                      QStringLiteral("QtCurve"),
                                                      QStandardPaths::LocateDirectory);
+        dirs += QStandardPaths::locateAll(QStandardPaths::GenericConfigLocation,
+                                          QStringLiteral("QtCurve"),
+                                          QStandardPaths::LocateDirectory);
         for (const QString &dir: dirs) {
             const QDir d(dir);
             const QStringList fileNames = d.entryList(QStringList() << QStringLiteral("*" EXTENSION));
